 "headline": "Why Claude and ChatGPT launches keep speeding up, and who will decide how hard your AI thinks",
 "deck": "A new Claude every four weeks, and ChatGPT from GPT-5.1 to 6.1 in under a year. Does the name matter, why is it speeding up, and why I think the choice of how hard your AI thinks is about to be made for you.",
 "date": "2026-10-16",
 "issue": "The headliner",
 "body": "body.md",
 "figures": [
  {
   "after": "Start with why your eyes are on the name at all, because while we watch the names, the setting that decides your answer gets chosen out of sight.",
   "image": "img/launches.png",
   "alt": "Anthropic and OpenAI launched a new model about every two weeks for a year: 6 launches in 16 days at the end."
  },
  {
   "after": "The size of the gear change surprised me.",
   "image": "img/model-or-thinking-level.png",
   "alt": "Turning up the thinking level lifted Claude and GPT more than a new version did."
  },
  {
   "after": "It isn't a straight line, though, and that matters for where this is heading.",
   "image": "img/each-step-buys-less.png",
   "alt": "Each step up in thinking buys Claude and GPT less for every extra dollar."
  },
  {
   "after": "That's also why a higher gear eats into your plan faster.",
   "image": "img/new-version-or-more-thinking.png",
   "alt": "A new Claude Opus or GPT Sol adds fewer points than more thinking, but costs less."
  },
  {
   "after": "If you build products on AI, don't choose a model by its name or its launch chart",
   "image": "img/cheapest-route-to-each-score.png",
   "alt": "The cheapest route to each score mixes Claude and GPT models and thinking levels."
  },
  {
   "after": "So the gear matters most on hard jobs, like Sally's contract.",
   "image": "img/smaller-claude-turned-up.png",
   "alt": "Claude Sonnet 5.5 at Max, Xhigh and High, and Haiku 5.5 at Max, all outscore Claude Opus 5.5 at Low."
  }
 ],
